## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to translate a concrete log-routing bug into a CAPA program that scales across tenants and flags, including governance, measurability, and rollback.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence, lineage, owners
- Tenant-aware lifecycle with detect/contain/remediate/verify and SLAs
- REST API design for CAPA management with logs/traces and policy links
- Metrics: containment MTTC, recurrence rate per tenant
- RCA template and canary rollout plan for config changes

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example CAPA data model (TypeScript)
interface CAPA {
  id: string;
  issue: string;
  tenantId: string;
  evidence: string[]; // logId, traceId
  lineage: string[]; // [source, sink]
  owners: string[];
  severity: 'low'|'medium'|'high';
  status: 'open'|'in_progress'|'mitigated'|'verified';
  timestamps: { detected: string; closed?: string };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test containment and prevention at scale?
- How would you secure CAPA data access and auditability?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to craft a CAPA program for cross-tenant data exposure caused by authorization cache mishandling. Emphasizes data modeling, lifecycle governance, API design, observability across regions, and rollback safety.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence, containment, remediation, and audit logs
- Region-aware, tenant-scoped metrics and dashboards
- Minimal REST API design for CAPA lifecycle
- RCA templates and controlled canary rollout for remediation
- Safe rollback and rollback criteria during canary

## Code Example
```javascript
interface CAPA {
  id: string;
  incidentId: string;
  tenantId: string;
  service: string;
  resource: string;
  evidence: string[];
  containmentActions: string[];
  remediation: string;
  status: "detected" | "triaged" | "contained" | "remediated" | "verified" | "closed";
  region?: string;
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate the canary rollout criteria and rollback?
